  "id": "group-polarization",
  "term": "group polarization",
  "definition": "Group polarization is the tendency for people in a group to move toward a more extreme position on an issue after taking part in, or being exposed to, group discussion. In online settings, especially among like-minded people, this can intensify opinions and contribute to more extreme public discourse.",
